{
  "title": "Aamal of Laylat al-Mab'ath (27th Night)",
  "data": "After the Isha prayer, sleep, then wake at any hour before midnight.\nOffer a prayer of twelve units, two at a time. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and any short surah from [Surah Muhammad](A51) (47) to the end of the Qur'an.\nAfter the prayer, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), [Surah al-Falaq](A117), [Surah al-Nas](A118), [Surah al-Tawheed](A116), [Surah al-Kafirun](A113), [Surah al-Qadr](A101) and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) seven times each, then recite:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE LAM YATTAKHIDH WALADAA\nAll praise be to Allah Who has not taken to Himself a son,\nوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِي الْمُلْكِ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHOO SHAREEKUN FIL MULK\nWho has no partner in the Sovereignty\nوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ وَلِيٌّ مِنَ الذُّلِّ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHOO WALIYYUN MINADH DHULL\nnor has He any protecting friend through dependence.\nوَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِيْرًا\nWA KABBIRHU TAKBEERAA\nAnd magnify Him with all magnificence.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَسْاَلُكَ بِمَعَاقِدِ عِزِّكَ عَلٰى اَرْكَانِ عَرْشِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BIMA'AAQIDI I'ZZIKA A'LAA ARKAANI A'RSHIK\nO Allah, verily I beseech You in the name of the situations of Your Dignity on the pillars of Your Throne,\nوَمُنْتَهَى الرَّحْمَةِ مِنْ كِتَابِكَ\nWA MUNTAHAR RAHMATI MIN KITAABIK\nin the name of Your utmost mercy in Your Book,\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الْاَعْظَمِ الْاَعْظَمِ الْاَعْظَمِ\nWA BISMIKAL A'ZAMIL A'ZAMIL A'ZAM\nin the name of Your Name—the Greatest, the Greatest, the Greatest,\nوَذِكْرِكَ الْاَعْلَى الْاَعْلَى الْاَعْلٰى\nWA DHIKRIKAL A'LAL A'LAL A'LAA\nin the name of Your Mention—the Highest, the Highest, the Highest,\nوَبِكَلِمَاتِكَ التَّامَّاتِ\nWA BIKALIMAATIKAT TAAMMAAT\nand in the name of Your Words the perfect,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nto bless Muhammad and his Household\nوَاَنْ تَفْعَلَ بِيْ مَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهُ\nWA AN TAF'ALA BEE MAA ANTA AHLUH\nand do to me that which befits You.\nThen ask for what you need.\nIt is also recommended to perform ghusl on this night.",
  "merits": "The twenty-seventh night of Rajab is the night on which Prophet Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) was given the mission of promulgating the religion. This highly blessed night is called laylat al-mab'ath, which stands for the beginning of the Holy Prophet's Mission of promulgating the true religion of Almighty Allah.\n\nShaykh al-Tusi, in his book of Misbah al-Mutahajjid, has quoted Imam Muhammad al-Jawad (a.s.) as saying, “There is a night in Rajab, which carries for people fortune that is more preferable than whatever is subjected to sunlight. It is the twenty-seventh night of Rajab. The next morning was the beginning of the Holy Prophet's prophethood. Verily, one who does acts of worship at this night will have the reward of one who has worshipped Almighty Allah for sixty years.” When the Imam (a.s.) was asked about the rites to be done at this night, he described this prayer and supplication."
}
